  "session": "session_01FLwgbTSmGMrqsXkBDsiwfG (the parent's session; this run is mode:subagent, the round-1 finisher)",
  "premise_still_valid": true,
  "summary": "Round 1 verified at head 40fe66778, which the previous run pushed before a container restart killed it. Both REWORK asks are met. inferDriverTypeFromUrl refuses an opaque scheme (two or more characters and a colon, other than file: and sqlite:) with the same UnsupportedDriverError and sentence, and a one-letter drive stays a path. The sqlite and sqlite-wasm arms of resolveStorageDefinition translate sqlite: / sqlite:// through the runtime host's normalizeDatabaseUrl. Every gate, pin and measurement passed at that head, so this run wrote no code and pushed nothing. Beyond the asks, a *.wasm.db name now selects the WASM engine only for a file, so it no longer rescues an unrecognised scheme (deviations[0]). One new finding: the CLI host opens file://NAME at the filesystem root (out_of_scope_findings[0], open_questions[0]).",
