      "verdict": "met",
      "lines": "packages/cli/src/utils/storage-driver.ts:107 imports normalizeDatabaseUrl from @objectstack/runtime, so there is no second copy of the rule; :524 the sqlite arm, `normalizeDatabaseUrl(databaseUrl ?? ':memory:')`; :542 the sqlite-wasm arm, the same rule.",
      "pins": "driver-vocabulary-parity.test.ts:519-521 (sqlite://x.db, sqlite:x.db, sqlite:///var/lib/objectstack/x.db: the runtime host's sqliteFile equals the CLI host's config.filename, in dev and prod), plus :522 (sqlite://x.wasm.db). storage-driver.test.ts:274-277 (also SQLITE://x.db; displayUrl keeps the typed URL), :286.",
      "proof": "Ablation R1-B1 5 red, R1-B2 2 red. Public door at 40fe66778: sqlite://x.db boots to ready in dev and production and creates ./x.db in the probe directory, where base 683bf9587 resolved //x.db, the filesystem root.",
