    }
  },
  "tests": "At 40fe66778, every heavy run through os-verify-lock, each verdict read from its VERDICT command-exit line. (1) Closure build: turbo run build --filter=@objectstack/cli... --concurrency=2, exit 0, 61/61 cached. packages/cli/dist/utils/storage-driver.js carries the round-1 code, by on-disk counts: normalizeDatabaseUrl(databaseUrl 2, wasmFile 3, the opaque regex 1, the old sqlite: strip 0. (2) Unit layer, two shards: pnpm --filter @objectstack/cli exec vitest run --project unit --maxWorkers=2 --shard=1/2, 'Test Files 148 passed (148)', 'Tests 2464 passed (2464)'; --shard=2/2, 'Test Files 147 passed (147)', 'Tests 1953 passed (1953)'. Total 295 files, 4417 tests, against 4399 at 683bf9587. The integration layer is declared to CI: no integration-tier file, spawn entry or driver/kernel boot path is in the diff. (3) pnpm --filter @objectstack/cli typecheck: exit 0 ('check:test-typecheck: OK'). tsc --noEmit --listFiles names both changed test files (include src, no exclude). (4) The two pinned files: 'Tests 149 passed (149)', the baseline for the ablation legs.",
  "gates": "Local, at 40fe66778. node scripts/pm/dispatch-gates.mjs --commands --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack, with no paths, derived 64 commands from 4 paths off merge base 53646fc4b. Each ran in order, its exit captured before any pipe and recorded as 'CMD :: exit N': all 64 exited 0. That includes check:dual-build-cjs-loads ('110 published require entry point(s) across 68 package(s) load') and check:i18n-coverage ('OK (14 config(s), 621 baselined untranslated string(s), none new)'), the 2 NOT MEASURED in round 0. --ran: 'Run reconciliation — 64 derived, 64 run, 0 NOT-MEASURED, 0 UNRUN', exit 0. Its STALE TREE line reads 19 commits behind origin/main, with 4 derived-from files moved (discovery-routes anchor, check-route-envelope, record-recognisers, sdui-manifest record). Control: the same derivation over the same 4 paths in a throwaway detached tree at origin/main ec44cf60b printed the identical 64 commands (diff exit 0). pnpm exec eslint packages/cli --no-inline-config: exit 0, 696 files, 0 errors, 0 warnings (JSON formatter). pnpm --filter @objectstack/cli typecheck: exit 0. Not owed: check:dev-prereqs and check:skill-frame-freshness (no packages/spec or framework edit), and a script's own suite (no gate or tool script edited). test:repo is CI's. CI check-runs on 40fe66778, 40 in all. success (34): Auto Label, Build Core, Check Changeset, Check Documentation Links, Check PR Size, Dogfood Regression Gate, Flag docs affected by code changes, Governed Surface Queue Guard, Lint & Repo Gates, Lint · CI, release & engine gates, Lint · ESLint, Lint · PM dispatch-gates, Lint · docs & code guards, Lint · repo & tooling gates, Lint · scoped · query-options erasure, Lint · scoped · slot lookup & corpus, Lint · scoped · tooling self-tests, No other open PR may claim the same issue, No other open PR may claim the same single-writer path, Part-of PR must not also close its card, Test Core, Test Core (1/6) to (6/6), The card this PR closes must claim this branch, Type Check · consumer gates, Type Check · debt ledger, Type Check · source gates, Type Check · workspace, TypeScript Type Check, filter. skipped (6): Build Docs, Console Pin Gate, Dogfood Regression Gate (matrix shard), Dogfood Verify CLI, Packed-tarball smoke (opt-in), Temporal Conformance (live PG + MySQL). None red, and none in progress.",
  "ablation": [
    "Tool: scripts/ablation-replace.mjs in WRAP mode, the wrapped command being the two pinned files under os-verify-lock. The subject is src, because both files import ./storage-driver.js relatively, so no dist/ is involved. Every leg: the tool proved the mutation on disk (anchor x1 → x0, a new blob) and the restore (blob == HEAD 893ea05be3ed, git diff HEAD empty). An outer trap in the leg script proved the restore again by hash and diff, and an on-disk grep found 0 ABLATION markers after each leg. Baseline 149 passed.",
    "R1-A, the opaque-scheme refusal: the opaque fallback deleted from the scheme test. 6 red / 143 green, the jdbc:postgresql://..., redis:cache and jdbc:x/app.wasm.db rows in both files.",
    "R1-A2, the drive boundary (added; see deviations): the opaque test widened from + to * (one-letter schemes). 2 red: C:\\data\\app and C:/data/app (storage-driver.test.ts:93).",
    "R1-B1, the alias translation in the sqlite arm: normalizeDatabaseUrl replaced by base's .replace(/^sqlite:/, ''). 5 red: sqlite://x.db and sqlite:///var/lib/objectstack/x.db in both files, and SQLITE://x.db. sqlite:x.db stays green, because base's strip already handled it.",
    "R1-B2, the alias translation in the sqlite-wasm arm, same mutation: 2 red, the sqlite://x.wasm.db rows in both files.",
    "R1-C, the .wasm.db-only-for-a-file rule: the *.wasm.db test moved back above every scheme check. 4 red: redis://h/app.wasm.db and jdbc:x/app.wasm.db in both files."
  ],
  "before_after": {
    "fixture": "the built CLI (node packages/cli/bin/run.js serve objectstack.config.mjs [--dev] --port RANDOM) over a throwaway HOST config: one object and one plain-object plugin with init, no imports. The cwd is a fresh directory under the scratch dir, NODE_ENV and OS_DATABASE_DRIVER unset, OS_CLOUD_URL=off, an auth secret set, timeout 60 s, killed on 'Server is ready'. Before = 683bf9587: storage-driver.ts restored to that commit in the worktree (unstaged, swap proven by blob 8100f9353946), built (dist counts: normalizeDatabaseUrl 0, wasmFile 0, opaque regex 0, sqlite: strip 2), then restored to HEAD (blob 893ea05be3ed == HEAD, git diff HEAD empty, porcelain empty) and rebuilt (61/61 cached, dist counts back to 2/3/1/0). After = 40fe66778, built.",
